+# Idempotent in Software
+
+An idempotent operation is one that produces the same result when executed multiple times as it does when executed once, regardless of how many times it is called. This property is critical for building reliable systems—for example, if a payment button is idempotent, clicking it repeatedly still charges the card only once.
+
+## Sources
+
